# --- worlds ---
node_modules/
# ...and as a symlink: kyoto-higashiyama/node_modules pointed at an absolute
# path on the author's machine, which the trailing-slash rule above does not
# match, so it was tracked as a 120000 blob and broke on every clone.
node_modules
dist/
.venv/
qa/shots/
qa/compare/
qa/walkthrough/
qa/demo/frames*/
qa/demo/*.mp4
src/data/recon/osm_raw.json
# Leading **/ for the same reason as the media/frames rule below: a pattern
# containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding this .gitignore, so a
# plain `refs/**/*.jpg` only ever matched a repo-root refs/ that does not exist —
# union-square-sf/refs/*.jpg was never actually ignored.
**/refs/**/*.jpg
**/refs/**/*.png
**/refs/**/*.jpeg
**/refs/**/*.webp
**/refs/**/*.tif
**/refs/**/*.tiff
**/refs/**/*.gif
.DS_Store

# Tour film: the recorded frames are an intermediate (gigabytes of PNG); the
# encoded mp4 / gif / stills in media/ ARE committed.
# Leading **/ because a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory
# holding the .gitignore -- plain `media/frames/` would only match the repo
# root's, never `kyoto-higashiyama/media/frames/`.
**/media/frames/
**/media/storyboard/
**/media/_*
**/qa/shots/

# --- ingest ---
# HTTP + DuckDB result cache. Content-addressed, safe to delete; `ingest build`
# refetches. Keeping it out of the tree is what makes the pipeline cheap to re-run.
.ingest-cache/

# Reference photography is fetched on demand by `ingest refs <world>`, never
# committed — we do not redistribute other people's photographs. The manifest that
# reproduces it (refs/*/SOURCES.md and .json) IS committed, so a clean clone can
# regenerate the camera-match ground truth.
!**/refs/**/SOURCES.md
!**/refs/**/SOURCES.json

# Generated by `ingest build <world>`, ~5 MB pretty-printed. Not committed: it is
# fully regenerable from ingest/worlds/<world>.json, and keeping it out of the tree
# is the point — the manifest is the artefact, the dataset is the output. The
# worlds still load their existing src/data/recon/*.json at runtime; wiring them to
# consume ingest.json is the next step, not part of this change.
**/src/data/recon/ingest.json
**/src/data/recon/UNCERTAINTY.md
